%description:
Tests minshallNagle=true when the sequence numbers wrap: the client has an
ISS of 4294965795, so its data crosses sequence number 0. The client writes
2500 bytes. After the ACK of t=1.203, the tail of 500 bytes goes at once after
the second full segment, as in tcp_nagle_minshall_1: no small segment was
sent, so none holds (Linux tcp_connect_init() sets snd_sml to the ISS).

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.cli_app.sendScript="1.0 2500"
*.*_tcp.mss = 1000
*.cli_tcp.minshallNagle = true
*.cli_tcp.initialSendSequenceNumber = 4294965795

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[1.203 B002] A.1000 < B.2000: A ack 4294966796 win 16384 
[1.205 A004] A.1000 > B.2000: A 4294966796:500(1000) ack 501 win 16384 
[1.205 A005] A.1000 > B.2000: A 500:1000(500) ack 501 win 16384 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
